# The `authors:` list below is deliberately EMPTY. It must not be guessed.
#
# Reason: this repository does not state an author anywhere authoritative.
#   - `LICENSE` is the unmodified Apache-2.0 text and its appendix still reads
#     "Copyright [yyyy] [name of copyright owner]", i.e. no holder is named.
#   - `README.md` names no author.
#   - The only signal is the GitHub account that owns the repository
#     (github.com/fanat503/rope-attribution). That is a handle, not a person,
#     and a legal attribution needs a real name.
# An earlier revision of this file cited two conflicting candidates ("fanat503"
# and "Vitebsk Research") from a now-removed self-referential patch; that file
# has been deleted, and neither candidate was ever authoritative.
#
# ACTION REQUIRED before tagging a release or publishing:
#   1. Replace `authors: []` below with the real author list, e.g.
#        authors:
#          - family-names: "<family name>"
#            given-names: "<given name>"
#            orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
#   2. Fill in the same name in the `LICENSE` appendix, which is still the
#      unfilled Apache-2.0 boilerplate.
#   3. Delete this comment block.
#   4. Re-run a CFF validator; `authors` is a required field, so the file will
#      not pass validation until it is non-empty.
#
# A placeholder name was deliberately NOT inserted: a wrong attribution in a
# legal document is worse than a missing one that fails validation loudly.

cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: >-
  If you use the reference implementations, experiments, or documents in this
  repository, please cite the RoFormer paper, which introduces the rotary
  position embedding the work is built on and is given below under
  preferred-citation, and also the YaRN paper, given below under references.
  Please also cite this repository itself once the author list above has been
  filled in.
title: "Attributing RoPE: exact score attribution, and what actually limits it"
